---
import ToolingLayout from "../../layouts/ToolingLayout.astro";
import CopyableCode from "../../components/CopyableCode.astro";
import { InsetText } from "@i-dot-ai-npm/component-library-astro";
---

<ToolingLayout title="Set up a project" currentPath="/tooling/set-up-agents">
  <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">Set up a project</h1>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Before you start, make sure you have{" "}
    <a href="/tooling/opencode" class="govuk-link">
      set up OpenCode with AI Gateway
    </a>
    .
  </p>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    A project is a dedicated workspace for a specific task or area. To set up a
    project for OpenCode, you need to:
  </p>

  <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>
      <a href="#create-project-folder" class="govuk-link">
        create a project folder
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="#create-project-agent" class="govuk-link">
        create a project-specific agent
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      (optional){" "}
      <a href="#create-project-memory" class="govuk-link">
        create project memory
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      (optional){" "}
      <a href="/tooling/add-and-use-skills" class="govuk-link">
        create project-specific skills
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="#use-your-project" class="govuk-link">
        use your project
      </a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="create-project-folder">
    Create a project folder
  </h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Your project files are stored in a folder. Create it somewhere easy to find,
    so you can add files later.
  </p>

  <p class="govuk-body">To set up a project folder:</p>

  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      Go to your <strong>Documents</strong> folder, right-click and select{" "}
      <strong>New folder</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>Name your project (you can use underscores but no spaces).</li>
    <li>Add any files or resources your project needs.</li>
  </ol>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    You can organise your files in subfolders if you want to.
  </p>

  <InsetText>
    OpenCode does not read all file formats. Use plain-text files, such as
    Markdown (.md), .txt and .csv or export to PDF.
  </InsetText>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="create-project-agent">
    Create a project-specific agent
  </h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Agents are text files with prompt instructions for the AI to follow. To make
    a project-specific agent:
  </p>

  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      Open Terminal, type:
      <CopyableCode code="cd " />
    </li>
    <li>
      Drag your project folder into the Terminal window to add the file path,
      and press return.
    </li>
    <li>
      To create a folder for your agent, in Terminal, run:
      <CopyableCode code="mkdir -p .opencode/agents" />
    </li>
    <li>
      To create your agent file, run:
      <CopyableCode code="code .opencode/agents/<agent-name>.md" />
      where <code class="app-code app-code--variable">
        &lt;agent-name&gt;
      </code>{" "}
      is the name of the agent (use lowercase and hyphens or underscores, not
      spaces).
    </li>
    <li>
      Copy and paste the template into the file:
      <CopyableCode
        code={`---
description: <DESCRIPTION>
mode: primary
model: litellm/bedrock-claude-sonnet-4-5-eu
permission:
  edit: deny
  bash: deny
  external_directory: deny
---

<INSTRUCTIONS>`}
      />
    </li>
    <li>
      Edit the template for your needs:
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>
          replace{" "}
          <code class="app-code app-code--variable">&lt;DESCRIPTION&gt;</code>{" "}
          with a short description of what the agent does
        </li>
        <li>
          change <code class="app-code">mode</code> to{" "}
          <code class="app-code">primary</code> (cycle with tab) or{" "}
          <code class="app-code">subagent</code> (invoked by other agents or
          with @mention)
        </li>
        <li>
          change the model if you want it to always use a specific one, or
          delete the line to use whichever model you have selected
        </li>
        <li>
          change the permissions (<code class="app-code">edit</code>,{" "}
          <code class="app-code">bash</code>,{" "}
          <code class="app-code">external_directory</code>) to{" "}
          <code class="app-code">allow</code>, <code class="app-code">ask</code>
          , or <code class="app-code">deny</code>
        </li>
        <li>
          replace{" "}
          <code class="app-code app-code--variable">&lt;INSTRUCTIONS&gt;</code>{" "}
          with your prompt instructions
        </li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li>Save the file.</li>
    <li>
      Check it works:
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>open Terminal and navigate to your project folder</li>
        <li>
          run <code class="app-code">opencode</code> to start OpenCode
        </li>
        <li>
          press <code class="app-code">tab</code> to see available agents - your
          new agent should appear
        </li>
      </ul>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h3 class="govuk-heading-m">Example agent</h3>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    This example creates a content review agent saved as{" "}
    <code class="app-code">content-review.md</code>:
  </p>

  <CopyableCode
    code={`---
description: Reviews content against GOV.UK style guidelines
mode: primary
model: litellm/bedrock-claude-sonnet-4-5-eu
permission:
  edit: deny
  bash: deny
  external_directory: ask
---

You are a GOV.UK content designer. Review any content I share against GOV.UK style guidelines. Flag issues and suggest improvements.

Use plain English, short sentences, and active voice.`}
  />

  <p class="govuk-body">
    This example is illustrative, and the description has been shortened.
  </p>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="create-project-memory">
    Create project memory
  </h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    OpenCode does not remember previous sessions. Each new session starts fresh.
    To make sure your agent remembers between sessions:
  </p>

  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      Open Terminal, type:
      <CopyableCode code="cd " />
    </li>
    <li>
      Drag your project folder into the Terminal window to add the file path,
      and press return.
    </li>
    <li>
      To make your notes file, run:
      <CopyableCode code="touch notes.md" />
    </li>
    <li>
      To open your agent instructions, run:
      <CopyableCode code="code .opencode/agents/<agent-name>.md" />
    </li>
    <li>
      At the start of your instructions, add:
      <CopyableCode
        code={`At the start of each session, read notes.md.

Update notes.md after you finish a task or we make a decision. Keep these sections:
- Current status: where the work is now
- Decisions: what we decided and why
- Next steps: what still needs to be done

Replace out-of-date information rather than adding to it.`}
      />
    </li>
    <li>Save the file.</li>
  </ol>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    To use memory, ask the AI to "update the notes" at the end of each session.
    To review and edit notes, run:
  </p>

  <CopyableCode code="code notes.md" />

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="use-your-project">
    Use your project
  </h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">To use your project:</p>

  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      Open Terminal, type:
      <CopyableCode code="cd " />
    </li>
    <li>
      Drag your project folder into the Terminal window to add the file path,
      and press return.
    </li>
    <li>
      To start OpenCode, run:
      <CopyableCode code="opencode" />
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p class="govuk-body">You start with 2 agents every time you use OpenCode:</p>

  <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>
      <strong>Plan</strong> - use this by default, it will ask you before making
      any changes to files
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Build</strong> - use this to create or edit files
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Press <code class="app-code">tab</code> to switch between agents. Your
    project-specific agents will also appear here.
  </p>

  <h3 class="govuk-heading-m">Change sessions</h3>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Each conversation you have with AI is called a session. To switch between
    sessions:
  </p>

  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
    <li>
      Open Terminal, type:
      <CopyableCode code="cd " />
    </li>
    <li>
      Drag your project folder into the Terminal window to add the file path,
      and press return.
    </li>
    <li>
      To start OpenCode, run:
      <CopyableCode code="opencode" />
    </li>
    <li>
      To view available sessions, type:
      <CopyableCode code="/sessions" />
    </li>
  </ol>
</ToolingLayout>
